,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":339.075424064,"data":"SCIENTIFIC FINDINGS \u0026 METHODOLOGICAL DISCLOSURES:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":339.075429448,"data":"1. Format Adaptation: MultiScaleScientificCANPipeline adapts raw hex payload bytes (DATA0..DATA7) into numeric channels.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":339.07543419,"data":"   NOTE: Because Car-Hacking lacks decoded wheel speed, coolant, or lighting signals, higher-order physical invariants operate in fallback mode.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":339.075439091,"data":"2. Injection Attacks vs Masquerade: Deep SVDD achieves 0.9821 Macro ROC-AUC (and 0.9990 on DoS), while Inception achieves 0.9008 Macro ROC-AUC.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":339.075443954,"data":"   Injection floods violate message timing (IAT) and payload distributions far more severely than ROAD stealth masquerade attacks (~0.88 AUC).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":339.075448952,"data":"3. Threshold Transfer Breakdown: On RPM Spoofing, Inception CNN suffers complete specificity collapse (Specificity = 0.0000 at P95),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":339.075454517,"data":"   flagging all windows as anomalous due to baseline shift. Conversely, Deep SVDD maintains 97.51% Specificity and 0.9990 AUC.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":339.075459357,"data":"4. DoS Dynamics: On DoS attacks, Inception achieves 0.9272 ROC-AUC but suffers poor thresholded recall (P95 Recall = 1.3%),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":339.075486983,"data":"   whereas Bias-Free Deep SVDD reaches 0.9990 ROC-AUC and 98.81% Recall, demonstrating the superiority of latent hyperspheres over MSE.\n"}
